-- title:
--   The loading velocity is supported near the segment it travels
-- statement:
--   Let $p_*=(4,0,0)$, $z\in\mathbb R^3$ and $\eta>0$. The loading velocity translates a neighbourhood of $p_*$ rigidly along the path $p_*+\sigma(t)(z-p_*)$, where $\sigma$ rises smoothly from $0$ to $1$. Let $K$ be the closed $2\eta$-enlargement of the box with opposite corners $p_*$ and $z$. Then
--   $$
--   u_{\mathrm{load}}(t,x)=0\qquad\text{for all }t\text{ and all }x\notin K .
--   $$
--
--   So the loading phase has a compact spatial support that depends only on $z$ and $\eta$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/Loading.lean#L106-L120

